    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d499">

                <pb facs="0839" n="711" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg711"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">738.3915/372</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Young</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-11-13"><hi rendition="#italic">November 13,
                        1928</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received November 24.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1091</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Supplementing the Legation’s despatch No.
                    1090, of November 10, 1928,<anchor n="86" xml:id="d499-f1"/> I have the honor to
                    forward for the Department’s <pb facs="0840" n="712" xml:id="pg712"/>
                    confidential information a translation of the projected Dominican-Haitian
                    boundary treaty.<anchor n="87" xml:id="d499-f2"/> The text of the treaty has
                    been informally agreed upon, but it has not yet been made public.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Evan E. Young</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d499-f1" n="86" xml:id="d499-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d499-f2" n="87" xml:id="d499-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed. For text of the treaty as signed at Santo Domingo, Jan. 21, 1929,
                    see League of Nations Treaty Series, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">cv</hi>,
                    p. 193. Ratifications were exchanged at Santo Domingo, Apr. 29, 1929.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
